dear mr. Cameron I'm writing this from  the heart from my cottage in moorland  which my husband and I have worked so  hard to make a comfortable home the  waters are not in yet but I can look out  of every window and see that the drains  are no longer doing their job the rena  at the bottom of the garden is full the  road here is flooded across right next  to me and it is only a matter of time  where that i'll have to move out I fear  for our house and possessions but there  is only so much that one can do to  protect them I do strongly believe that  this catastrophe which has so badly  affected our hard-working farmers and  their livelihood as well as the  villagers here this could have been  avoided if help had been given sooner at  Christmas and as and as well over the  last few years that's when we needed it  please help us all for the future dear  Mr Cameron I write this letter as flood  water is slowly approaching our home the  majority of our village is already under  water as is the rest of the Somerset  Levels  why oh why when we had the floods last  year did you not start maintenance then  I can't believe that you were naive  enough to believe that it would not  happen again  the money you are setting aside will  this also include plans to reimburse the  poor souls who have lost so much will  consideration be given to reducing our  contribution to overseas aid there are  many in our village wondering about the  saying charity begins at home and  finally I understand that today you  visited Birmingham was this an important  meeting more important than coming to  see us here in Moreland
 

